722
00:24:45,162 --> 00:24:45,522
goals.

723
00:24:45,702 --> 00:24:47,660
A low rate mortgage might be fine

724
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:49,143
to keep while you invest,

725
00:24:49,143 --> 00:24:51,220
while a high rate mortgage might be

726
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:52,703
worth paying down faster.

727
00:24:53,052 --> 00:24:55,353
A paid off home also gives you

728
00:24:55,353 --> 00:24:55,967
options.

729
00:24:56,147 --> 00:24:59,386
Some retirees downsize and invest the difference.

730
00:24:59,566 --> 00:25:01,472
Others use a reverse mortgage,

731
00:25:01,472 --> 00:25:03,823
a loan that lets homeowners sixty two

732
00:25:03,823 --> 00:25:06,111
and older convert part of their home

733
00:25:06,111 --> 00:25:07,318
equity into income,

734
00:25:07,318 --> 00:25:09,733
though these come with costs and rules

735
00:25:09,733 --> 00:25:11,512
that deserve careful review.

736
00:25:11,692 --> 00:25:12,545
And for many,

737
00:25:12,545 --> 00:25:15,103
simply having no housing payment is the

738
00:25:15,103 --> 00:25:17,857
greatest financial peace of mind there is.

739
00:25:18,207 --> 00:25:19,067
Try this.

740
00:25:19,247 --> 00:25:21,751
Calculate how much lower your monthly expenses

741
00:25:21,751 --> 00:25:23,275
would be without a mortgage.

742
00:25:23,455 --> 00:25:25,493
That number shows how much income a

743
00:25:25,493 --> 00:25:27,240
paid off home is worth to you.

744
00:25:27,590 --> 00:25:28,984
Asset number fifteen.

745
00:25:29,164 --> 00:25:30,847
Delayed Social Security.

746
00:25:31,197 --> 00:25:33,998
Social Security pays monthly for life and

747
00:25:33,998 --> 00:25:35,501
adjusts for inflation,

748
00:25:35,501 --> 00:25:38,165
features that would be expensive to buy

749
00:25:38,165 --> 00:25:38,848
privately.

750
00:25:39,028 --> 00:25:40,065
For many people,

751
00:25:40,065 --> 00:25:43,045
it's their most valuable monthly income asset.

752
00:25:43,395 --> 00:25:45,397
You can claim as early as sixty

753
00:25:45,397 --> 00:25:48,109
two, but benefits are permanently reduced.

754
00:25:48,289 --> 00:25:50,524
For each year you delay past full

755
00:25:50,524 --> 00:25:52,827
retirement age, up to age seventy,

756
00:25:52,827 --> 00:25:55,603
benefits increase by about eight percent,

757
00:25:55,603 --> 00:25:58,854
according to the Social Security Administration.

758
00:25:59,204 --> 00:26:00,911
Delaying isn't right for everyone.

759
00:26:01,091 --> 00:26:04,504
Health, other savings and marriage all matter.

760
00:26:04,684 --> 00:26:06,014
But for many people,

761
00:26:06,014 --> 00:26:08,739
especially those who expect to live long,

762
00:26:08,739 --> 00:26:12,196
delaying can significantly increase lifetime income.

763
00:26:12,546 --> 00:26:15,067
Some retirees use savings to cover the

764
00:26:15,067 --> 00:26:18,649
years between retirement and claiming Social Security,

765
00:26:18,649 --> 00:26:21,567
effectively buying a larger lifetime income.

766
00:26:21,917 --> 00:26:22,962
Here's an example.

767
00:26:23,142 --> 00:26:25,765
Someone with a full retirement age benefit

768
00:26:25,765 --> 00:26:28,075
