780
00:26:51,955 --> 00:26:54,003
full retirement age and seventy.

781
00:26:54,353 --> 00:26:55,886
Now let's put it all together.

782
00:26:56,066 --> 00:26:58,895
Here's how many people build monthly income

783
00:26:58,895 --> 00:27:01,198
in layers, from safest to riskiest.

784
00:27:01,547 --> 00:27:03,846
Layer one is your emergency fund,

785
00:27:03,846 --> 00:27:06,215
in a high yield savings account or

786
00:27:06,215 --> 00:27:07,469
money market fund.

787
00:27:07,649 --> 00:27:09,825
It pays a little monthly interest,

788
00:27:09,825 --> 00:27:12,449
but its real job is protecting everything

789
00:27:12,449 --> 00:27:12,769
else.

790
00:27:12,949 --> 00:27:15,614
Without it, an unexpected bill can force

791
00:27:15,614 --> 00:27:17,747
you to sell investments at a bad

792
00:27:17,747 --> 00:27:18,080
time.

793
00:27:18,430 --> 00:27:20,945
Layer two is guaranteed income,

794
00:27:20,945 --> 00:27:22,649
like Social Security,

795
00:27:22,649 --> 00:27:25,083
a pension or a simple annuity.

796
00:27:25,263 --> 00:27:27,531
This covers your most basic expenses,

797
00:27:27,531 --> 00:27:29,860
so a market crash never threatens your

798
00:27:29,860 --> 00:27:32,066
ability to pay for food and housing.

799
00:27:32,416 --> 00:27:36,139
Layer three is your diversified investment portfolio,

800
00:27:36,139 --> 00:27:38,035
stock and bond index funds,

801
00:27:38,035 --> 00:27:40,915
producing dividends, interest and growth.

802
00:27:41,095 --> 00:27:45,072
This covers lifestyle expenses and protects against

803
00:27:45,072 --> 00:27:46,865
inflation over decades.

804
00:27:47,215 --> 00:27:50,182
Layer four is optional ownership income,

805
00:27:50,182 --> 00:27:51,740
like rental property,

806
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:53,520
a business or royalties.

807
00:27:53,700 --> 00:27:54,844
These can add a lot,

808
00:27:54,844 --> 00:27:56,676
but they come with more work and

809
00:27:56,676 --> 00:27:56,962
risk.

810
00:27:57,312 --> 00:27:59,532
Here's a simple example of the layers

811
00:27:59,532 --> 00:28:00,552
working together.

812
00:28:00,732 --> 00:28:03,482
A retired couple spends five thousand dollars

813
00:28:03,482 --> 00:28:03,971
a month.

814
00:28:04,151 --> 00:28:07,193
Social Security covers three thousand two hundred.

815
00:28:07,373 --> 00:28:10,420
Their diversified portfolio of about five hundred

816
00:28:10,420 --> 00:28:11,850
forty thousand dollars,

817
00:28:11,850 --> 00:28:13,467
withdrawn at four percent,

818
00:28:13,467 --> 00:28:16,266
covers about one thousand eight hundred more.

819
00:28:16,446 --> 00:28:18,527
Their emergency fund sits in a money

820
00:28:18,527 --> 00:28:19,221
market fund.

821
00:28:19,401 --> 00:28:20,833
Every layer has a job,

822
00:28:20,833 --> 00:28:22,917
and no single asset has to carry

823
00:28:22,917 --> 00:28:23,894
the whole load.

824
00:28:24,243 --> 00:28:26,127
In your twenties and thirties,

825
00:28:26,127 --> 00:28:28,764
monthly income from assets is mostly about

826
00:28:28,764 --> 00:28:29,329
planting.

827
00:28:29,509 --> 00:28:32,253
Your emergency fund earns a little interest,

828
00:28:32,253 --> 00:28:35,497
and your retirement accounts reinvest every dividend

829
00:28:35,497 --> 00:28:36,370
automatically.

830
00:28:36,550 --> 00:28:38,945
You probably don't need the income yet,

831
00:28:38,945 --> 00:28:41,217
so letting it compound is usually the

832
00:28:41,217 --> 00:28:42,077
smartest move.

833
00:28:42,257 --> 00:28:45,268
Every dividend reinvested now becomes a bigger

834
00:28:45,268 --> 00:28:46,250
dividend later.

835
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,406
In your forties and fifties,

836
00:28:48,406 --> 00:28:51,372
many people start shaping their future income.

837
00:28:51,552 --> 00:28:53,253
Paying down the mortgage,

838
00:28:53,253 --> 00:28:55,633
checking Social Security estimates,

839
00:28:55,633 --> 00:28:58,490
